MIAN AHMAD BASIT — ENTERPRISE AI ENGINEERING SPECIALIZATION SYLLABUS

=========================================
PHASE 0 — PROGRAMMING & AI FOUNDATIONS
=========================================

MODULE p0-mod-1: Python Syntax & Core Fundamentals
Deep dive into Python language constructs, data structures, and memory mechanics.

Topics:
- Core Syntax & Control Flow: Python syntax and fundamentals, Variables and data types, Operators (arithmetic, logical, bitwise), Conditional statements (if-elif-else), Loops (for, while, loop control break/continue)
- Functions & Functional Paradigms: Functions, arguments, *args, **kwargs, Lambda functions & anonymous execution, List, tuple, set and dictionary deep dive, Comprehensions (list, dict, set comprehensions), String manipulation & regex parsing
- File & Environment Management: File handling & context management, Exception handling (try-except-finally), Modules, packages, & relative imports, Virtual environments (venv, conda, poetry), Package management with pip & dependency locking

MODULE p0-mod-2: Object-Oriented & Advanced Python Paradigms
Advanced OOP principles, metaprogramming, type hints, and asynchronous Python.

Topics:
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP): Classes and objects mechanics, Inheritance (single, multiple, MRO), Encapsulation & private attributes, Polymorphism & duck typing, Abstraction & Abstract Base Classes (ABC)
- Advanced Python Mechanics: Iterators and custom iterable protocol, Generators & memory-efficient yield loops, Decorators & wrapper functions with state, Context managers (__enter__, __exit__), Type hints & static typing verification, Dataclasses & immutability
- Async Programming & API Integration: asyncio event loop fundamentals, async/await patterns & non-blocking execution, Concurrency fundamentals (tasks, gather, semaphores), HTTP/REST fundamentals & async requests, JSON serialization & deserialization, Environment variables management (.env), Git/GitHub basics & workflow, Python project structure & package setup


=========================================
MACHINE LEARNING FOUNDATIONS
=========================================

MODULE ml-mod-1: Mathematics for Machine Learning
The exact mathematical concepts that power vector spaces, optimization loss landscapes, and probabilistic models.

Topics:
- Linear Algebra: Scalars, Vectors, Matrices, and Tensors, Matrix operations (addition, transposition), Dot product, Vector Norms (L1, L2), Matrix multiplication mechanics, Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors
- Probability & Statistics: Probability fundamentals & Axioms, Conditional probability & Joint probability, Bayes theorem & Bayesian inference, Random variables (Discrete & Continuous), Probability distributions (Gaussian, Bernoulli, Poisson), Mean, Variance, Standard deviation, Covariance and Correlation matrices, Descriptive statistics vs Inferential statistics, Sampling techniques & Central Limit Theorem, Hypothesis testing & p-values, Confidence intervals
- Calculus & Optimization: Derivatives & rate of change, Partial derivatives & Gradient vectors, Gradients & Loss surface geometry, Chain rule for composite functions, Optimization fundamentals & Convexity

MODULE ml-mod-2: Classical Machine Learning Algorithms & Engineering
Supervised and Unsupervised learning, ensemble methods, feature engineering, and model evaluation.

Topics:
- Core ML Concepts & Taxonomy: What is Machine Learning?, Supervised Learning paradigm, Unsupervised Learning paradigm, Semi-supervised Learning, Reinforcement Learning overview
- Supervised Algorithms (Regression & Classification): Linear Regression & Ordinary Least Squares, Multiple Linear Regression, Polynomial Regression, Logistic Regression & Sigmoid Decision Boundaries, K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN), Naive Bayes Classifier, Decision Trees & Information Gain / Gini Impurity, Random Forest & Bagging, Gradient Boosting Machines (GBM), XGBoost, LightGBM, and CatBoost, Support Vector Machines (SVM), Support Vector Regression (SVR)
- Unsupervised Learning & Dimensionality Reduction: K-Means Clustering & Elbow Method, Hierarchical Clustering & Dendrograms, DBSCAN (Density-Based Spatial Clustering), Principal Component Analysis (PCA), Dimensionality Reduction techniques
- Feature Engineering & Data Pipeline: Feature Selection methods, Categorical Encoding (One-Hot, Target, Ordinal), Scaling: MinMax Normalization vs Standardization (Z-score), Missing Value Imputation strategies, Outlier Detection (IQR, Z-score, Isolation Forest), Data Leakage prevention, Train/Validation/Test Split strategies, K-Fold & Stratified Cross Validation
- Optimization, Tuning & Evaluation: Hyperparameter Tuning: Grid Search & Random Search, Confusion Matrix (TP, FP, TN, FN), Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1 Score, ROC-AUC & Precision-Recall (PR-AUC) Curves, Regression Metrics: MAE, MSE, RMSE, R², Bias-Variance Tradeoff, Underfitting vs Overfitting diagnostics, Regularization: L1 (Lasso) vs L2 (Ridge), Ensemble Learning techniques, Scikit-Learn Pipelines & Model Serialization (joblib/pickle), ML deployment fundamentals


=========================================
DEEP LEARNING FOUNDATIONS
=========================================

MODULE dl-mod-1: Neural Networks & Optimization Mechanics
Perceptrons, multi-layer networks, backpropagation calculus, and optimization algorithms.

Topics:
- Neural Network Architecture Basics: Artificial Neurons & Biological Inspiration, Perceptron model & Linearity limits, Forward Propagation through Dense Layers, Backpropagation & Computation Graphs, Loss Functions (MSE, Cross-Entropy, Binary Cross-Entropy)
- Optimization Algorithms & Initializations: Gradient Descent & Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD), Mini-batch Gradient Descent, Momentum & Nesterov Accelerated Gradient, Adam & AdamW Optimizers, Learning Rate Scheduling (Cosine Annealing, Warmup), Weight Initialization: Xavier / Glorot Initialization, Weight Initialization: He / Kaiming Initialization
- Activations, Normalization & Regularization: Activation Functions: Sigmoid, Tanh, ReLU, Leaky ReLU, GELU, Softmax, Batch Normalization (BatchNorm), Layer Normalization (LayerNorm), Dropout & DropPath Regularization, L1/L2 Regularization in Neural Networks, Vanishing Gradients & Exploding Gradients problems

MODULE dl-mod-2: PyTorch, CNNs & Sequence Models
Hands-on PyTorch engineering, Convolutional Networks for Vision, and Recurrent Architectures for Sequences.

Topics:
- PyTorch Framework Fundamentals: PyTorch Tensors & Memory Layout, Autograd automatic differentiation engine, Building custom models with nn.Module, Dataset & DataLoader custom implementations, Training loops & Validation loops, GPU Acceleration (CUDA/MPS execution), Mixed Precision Training (torch.cuda.amp), Model Checkpointing & State Dicts, Transfer Learning workflows
- Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs): Convolution operation, Kernels, & Filters, Feature Maps, Stride, & Padding math, Pooling operations: Max Pooling & Average Pooling, Classic CNN Architectures (ResNet, EfficientNet), Transfer Learning for Computer Vision, Image Classification pipelines
- Sequence Models & Recurrent Architectures: Recurrent Neural Networks (RNN), Vanishing Gradient Problem in RNNs, Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) Networks, Gated Recurrent Units (GRU), Bidirectional RNNs, Sequence-to-Sequence (Seq2Seq) Architectures, Encoder-Decoder Paradigms, Teacher Forcing technique, Introduction to Attention Mechanism


=========================================
NLP FOUNDATIONS
=========================================

MODULE nlp-mod-1: NLP Core Concepts & Vector Spaces
Text representation techniques from lexical features to dense continuous vector spaces.

Topics:
- Text Preprocessing Pipelines: Natural Language Processing fundamentals, Text Normalization (lowercasing, unicode handling), Tokenization methods, Stopwords removal, Stemming (Porter, Snowball) vs Lemmatization (WordNet), N-grams language representations, Bag of Words (BoW) model, TF-IDF (Term Frequency - Inverse Document Frequency)
- Word Embeddings & Dense Representations: Word Embeddings intuition, Word2Vec Architecture: Continuous Bag of Words (CBOW), Word2Vec Architecture: Skip-Gram with Negative Sampling, GloVe (Global Vectors for Word Representation), Contextual Embeddings evolution
- Downstream NLP Tasks: Sequence classification paradigms, Text classification & Topic Modeling, Named Entity Recognition (NER), Sentiment Analysis & Intent Recognition, Language modeling fundamentals, Seq2Seq for Translation & Summarization, Attention Mechanism in NLP, Introduction to the Transformer Architecture


=========================================
01 — AI FOUNDATIONS & TRANSFORMERS 101
=========================================

MODULE 01-mod-1: Transformers 101 & Attention Mechanism
Mathematical intuition and PyTorch implementation of the Transformer block.

Topics:
- Embeddings: Discrete to Continuous Space: High-dimensional semantic spaces, Embedding lookup tables & projection matrices, Cosine similarity & Dot product spaces
- The Attention Mechanism Deep Dive: Scaled Dot-Product Attention (Q, K, V math), Self-Attention computation step-by-step, Multihead Attention (MHA) & Parallel subspace projection, Masked Multihead Attention (Autoregressive causal mask), Positional Encoding (Sinusoidal vs Learned), Encoder–Decoder Transformers (Original Vaswani et al.), Encoder-Only Transformers (BERT, RoBERTa), Decoder-Only Transformers (GPT series, LLaMA), Cross-Attention in Encoder-Decoder models

MODULE 01-mod-2: Tokenization Deep Dive
Subword algorithms, byte-level processing, vocabulary construction, and edge-case handling.

Topics:
- Taxonomy of Tokenization: Word level vs Subword level vs Character level vs Byte level, Byte Pair Encoding (BPE) algorithm step-by-step, WordPiece tokenization (BERT style), Unigram & SentencePiece tokenization, Byte-level BPE (tiktoken, LLaMA tokenizer), Special tokens (<unk>, <s>, </s>, <pad>, <mask|, system tokens)


=========================================
02 — PROMPTS TO PROGRAMS & PROGRAMMATIC LLMS
=========================================

MODULE 02-mod-1: Advanced Prompt Engineering Strategies
Systematic prompt design, chain-of-thought, meta-prompting, and output enforcement.

Topics:
- Prompt Architecture & Design Patterns: Anatomy of a Production Prompt, Zero-Shot, One-Shot, & Few-Shot Prompting strategies, Chain-of-Thought (CoT) & Step-Back Prompting, System Prompt Design & Role Assignment, Output Formatting & Structured Generation, Prompt Sensitivity & Robustness Testing, Prompt Chaining & Decomposition Strategies, Meta-Prompting & Self-Refinement Loops

MODULE 02-mod-2: Instructor, Pydantic & Outlines for Typed Outputs
Guarantee 100% schema-compliant responses using typed validation contracts and token masking.

Topics:
- Instructor — Structured Outputs with Pydantic: Why typed outputs matter in production, One-line client patching with Instructor, Pydantic models as execution contracts, Auto-retry loops with validation error context, Nested schemas, streaming validation, & async support, Mode system (TOOLS vs JSON_SCHEMA vs MD_JSON)
- Outlines — Guided Generation & Finite State Automata: FSA-based token masking at logits level, Pydantic + JSON Schema enforcement, Regex generation for strict formats, Context-free grammars for SQL, Code, & Custom DSLs

MODULE 02-mod-3: DSPy — Programmatic LLM Pipeline Optimization
Replacing manual prompt engineering with compiled, self-optimizing DSPy programs.

Topics:
- Core DSPy Abstractions: From Prompt Engineering to Programs, Signatures — Defining inputs and outputs declaratively, Modules — Predict, ChainOfThought, ReAct, ProgramOfThought, LM Configuration & Telemetry
- DSPy Optimizers (Teleprompters): BootstrapFewShot — Automatic few-shot example selection, BootstrapFewShotWithRandomSearch, MIPROv2 — Multi-prompt instruction proposal optimizer, SIMBA & GEPA optimizers, BetterTogether & BootstrapFinetune for model distillation


=========================================
03 — KV CACHE & ADVANCED ATTENTIONS
=========================================

MODULE 03-mod-1: Finetuning Transformer Architectures
Hands-on training of DistillBERT, DistillGPT, and T5 on custom task datasets.

Topics:
- Finetuning Core Architectures: Coding Attention Mechanisms in PyTorch, Finetuning DistillBERT for Classification with Custom Data, Finetuning DistillGPT for Generation with Custom Data, Finetuning T5 for Seq2Seq tasks with Custom Data

MODULE 03-mod-2: KV Cache & Modern Attention Variants
Optimizing inference speed and memory throughput using FlashAttention, GQA, MLA, and vLLM PagedAttention.

Topics:
- Memory Math & KV Cache: The Naive Decoding Problem (O(N^2) redundant computation), KV Cache mechanics & memory footprint calculation, FlashAttention 1, 2 & 3 — IO-awareness & GPU SRAM tiling, PyTorch SDPA — The Unified Scaled Dot-Product Attention API
- Architectural Attention Variants: Multi-Head Attention (MHA) memory bottleneck, Multi-Query Attention (MQA), Grouped-Query Attention (GQA) — LLaMA-3 standard, Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) — DeepSeek-V2/V3 standard, PagedAttention & vLLM virtual memory management, RoPE Positional Encoding (Rotary Position Embeddings)
- Scaling Laws & Compute Budgets: Scaling Laws for Neural Language Models (Kaplan et al.), Training Compute-Optimal LLMs (Chinchilla Scaling Laws), Tokens-to-parameters ratio & dataset scaling math


=========================================
04 — FINETUNING LANGUAGE MODELS & PEFT
=========================================

MODULE 04-mod-1: Pre-training vs Post-training Lifecycle & Data Prep
Understanding pre-training objectives, continued pre-training (CPT), and instruction dataset engineering.

Topics:
- Finetuning Lifecycle Foundations: Pre-training vs Post-training — the two-phase view, What pre-training produces (base model capabilities & limitations), Why base models are not useful out of the box, Training objectives recap: CLM, MLM, Prefix-LM
- Pre-Training Deep Dive & Continued Pre-Training: Data curation and filtering at scale (CommonCrawl, RefinedWeb), Continued Pre-Training (CPT) for domain adaptation, The compute budget problem & scaling law tradeoffs, When CPT is needed vs jumping straight to SFT, Multi-Token Prediction (MTP) architectures
- Data Preparation for Fine-Tuning: Dataset formats (instruction pairs, chat format), Chat templates: ChatML, LLaMA-3, Mistral formatting, Loss masking — why it matters, what breaks without it, Deduplication and filtering pipelines, Synthetic data generation (Self-Instruct, Alpaca-style)

MODULE 04-mod-2: PEFT Techniques: LoRA, QLoRA, DoRA & AdaLoRA
Parameter-efficient fine-tuning math, 4-bit NF4 quantization, and adapter architectures.

Topics:
- Parameter-Efficient Fine-Tuning (PEFT): The intrinsic dimensionality insight of neural weights, LoRA — Low-Rank Adaptation math (W = W0 + B*A, rank r, alpha scaling), QLoRA — 4-bit NormalFloat (NF4), Double Quantization, Paged Optimizers, DoRA — Weight-Decomposed Low-Rank Adaptation (magnitude + direction), AdaLoRA — Adaptive rank allocation across layers, LoRA+ — Separate learning rates for A and B projection matrices
- Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT): SFT as Stage 1 of every post-training pipeline, Instruction tuning (FLAN, Alpaca, OpenHermes datasets), Chat / conversational fine-tuning mechanics, Chain-of-Thought fine-tuning for reasoning, Domain-specific fine-tuning best practices

MODULE 04-mod-3: Preference Alignment & Advanced Post-Training
Aligning LLMs with human preferences using DPO, GRPO, ORPO, and RLHF.

Topics:
- Preference Alignment Paradigms: Why SFT alone is not enough (distribution shift & verbosity bias), RLHF with PPO — reward model, critic network, KL penalty calculation, DPO — Direct Preference Optimization (no reward model required), GRPO — Group Relative Policy Optimization (DeepSeek-Math/R1 approach), ORPO — Odds Ratio Preference Optimization (single-stage, zero dependencies)
- Quantization & Deployment Prep: Quantization standards: GPTQ, AWQ, BNB NF4, FP8, Merging LoRA adapters into base weights before serving, Inference frameworks: vLLM, SGLang, Serving multiple LoRA adapters dynamically from one base model, GGUF, GGUML format for CPU & local edge execution, llama.cpp engine optimization, Speculative Decoding & Inference acceleration
- Tooling & Frameworks: HuggingFace TRL — SFT, DPO, GRPO, ORPO trainers, Unsloth — 2x-5x faster training with custom GPU kernels, Axolotl — full YAML configurability for cluster training, LLaMA-Factory — no-code web UI for SFT and alignment, Together AI / AWS SageMaker managed fine-tuning
- Synthetic Dataset Generation: Why Data Is the Leverage Point in 2026, Taxonomy of Synthetic Data (Instruction vs Preference vs Code), Instruction Dataset Generation (Self-Instruct, Alpaca: Scaling Self-Instruct), Preference Dataset Generation (LLM-as-Judge Scoring), Tools: distilabel, DataDreamer, Argilla, Risks: Model Collapse and Data Poisoning prevention, End-to-End Pipeline: Building a Domain SFT Dataset


=========================================
05 — MIXTURE OF EXPERTS & REASONING MODELS
=========================================

MODULE 05-mod-1: Mixture of Experts (MoE) Architecture
Sparse gating, router load balancing, expert specialization, and production serving.

Topics:
- MoE Core Architecture: The Dense Model Scaling Problem (compute wall), The MoE Idea: Sparse activation of sub-networks, Architecture Deep Dive: Gating networks & Top-K router math, Load Balancing loss functions & Auxiliary loss, Training MoE Models at scale, Inference with MoE (memory vs compute tradeoffs), MoE Variants (Mixtral 8x7B, DeepSeek-V3 256 experts), Production MoE Models, MoE vs Dense: When to Use Each

MODULE 05-mod-2: Reasoning Models & DeepSeek-R1 Paradigm
Reinforcement learning for long-form reasoning, rule-based rewards, and model distillation.

Topics:
- Reasoning Models Architecture: What Is a Reasoning Model? (System 1 vs System 2 thinking), Chain-of-Thought: The Foundation for explicit reasoning traces, The Training Recipe: Pure RL vs SFT+RL, DeepSeek-R1-Zero: Skipping SFT Entirely with Rule-Based RL, Distillation: Reasoning Without RL (transferring CoT traces to SLMs)


=========================================
06 — KNOWLEDGE DISTILLATION & SMALL LANGUAGE MODELS
=========================================

MODULE 06-mod-1: Small Language Models (SLMs) & Edge AI
Building ultra-compact 1B-3B models with performance rivaling large LLMs.

Topics:
- SLM Design Philosophy: What Is a Small Language Model? (Phi-3, Gemma-2B, LLaMA-3.2-1B), Why SLMs Matter: Latency, privacy, edge deployment, cost, The SLM Design Philosophy — Data density over model size, Key Techniques for Building SLMs (high-quality data filtering, deep architectures), Liquid Foundation Models & Dynamical Systems, Training SLMs from Scratch vs Fine-Tuning, Fine-Tuning SLMs for specialized downstream tasks, Reasoning in SLMs with distilled traces, SLM vs LLM: Choosing the Right Scale for your problem

MODULE 06-mod-2: Knowledge Distillation Pipelines
Compressing teacher model knowledge into student networks using temperature scaling and KL loss.

Topics:
- Distillation Mathematics & Engineering: The Student-Teacher Paradigm explained, The Core Problem: What Is Knowledge?, Hard Labels vs Soft Labels probability distributions, Temperature Scaling in Softmax output, The KL Divergence Loss formulation, Attention Transfer & Hidden State Matching, Building a Distillation Pipeline:, — Step 1: Teacher Data & Logit Generation, — Step 2: Student Architecture Design, — Step 3: Training the Student Network


