Patch embeddings, 2D positional encodings, self-attention on visual tokens, and pre-trained encoders.

Topics:
- Vision Transformer (ViT) Architecture: From CNN to Vision Transformer — The Conceptual Bridge, ViT Architecture Deep Dive, Image as a Sequence of Patches (16x16 patch projection), Patch Embedding linear projection layer, The CLS Token for global image classification, Positional Encoding for 2D Spatial Inputs, Transformer Encoder execution on Visual Tokens, Attention Maps — What ViT Sees, CNN vs ViT — Inductive Bias and the Core Tradeoff
- Pre-Trained Vision Encoders: CLIP — Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training (OpenAI), SigLIP — Sigmoid Loss Variant for pair matching, DINO / DINOv2 — Self-Supervised Vision representation

